---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy — Burnished Sky Ahead"
  description="Privacy notice for Burnished Sky Ahead by devjoe."
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Current privacy notice</p>
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Burnished Sky Ahead reads selected Garmin-provided data on the watch. The current release does not send it to devjoe.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="content-grid">
      <aside>Data boundary</aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Data used on the watch</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Local time, date, device settings, battery, and charging state.</li>
          <li>Daily steps and calories, plus the latest cached heart-rate sample.</li>
          <li>Garmin-cached current weather and hourly forecasts.</li>
          <li>An available cached position used to calculate sunrise and sunset.</li>
          <li>Garmin’s alarm and Do Not Disturb state when the device exposes it.</li>
          <li>Garmin’s notification count when the optional Show notification count setting is enabled.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Processing and transmission</h2>
        <p>
          The current release has no Communications permission, developer server,
          advertising SDK, analytics SDK, account system, or developer telemetry.
          It does not send the data above to devjoe.
        </p>
        <p>
          The watch face does not display coordinates or transmit, serialize, or
          write them to release logs. Status values are processed locally and
          are used only to decide whether the compact indicators are visible.
        </p>
        <h2>Stored preferences</h2>
        <p>
          Garmin’s application-properties system stores only watch-face
          preferences, including AOD ornament, weather-frame style, Outdoor
          Brief mode, Weather Signals choices, and the default-off Show
          notification count setting.
        </p>
        <h2>External support</h2>
        <p>
          The support page may link to GitHub and Ko-fi. Those services have their
          own privacy terms. The watch face does not send Garmin data, device
          identifiers, settings, usage history, or Tip status to either service.
        </p>
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 2026-01-01</p>
        </div>
        <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:support@devjoe.app">support@devjoe.app</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
